00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:43.620
So hope you see some kind of difference.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:46.100
The Easter holidays for me are a great way

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:49.620
to reconnect with myself,
with my family and my friends.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:53.140
Hope you also had a similar
great experience at home.

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:55.580
I know the current times are difficult.

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:58.070
It is going to be a very
special Easter holiday

00:00:58.070 --> 00:00:59.110
for most of us.

00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:01.840
In the last days I tried
to work on a few things,

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:04.470
I set up my Instagram
channel for you again,

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:07.210
I'm currently posting several
pieces of content there

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:08.360
every single day.

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:10.390
So let me know if you
have any feedback for me,

00:01:10.390 --> 00:01:12.370
I would highly appreciate your views.

00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:15.390
But now back to the studio
and welcome once again

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:17.420
to another coffee break
with Firm Learning.

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:19.630
For those of you who are regular watchers

00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:21.240
and subscribers of this channel,

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:22.720
thank you so much for your time.

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:24.760
And for those of you
watched the first time

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:27.400
first of all, welcome my name is Heinrich

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:28.750
and here on Firm Learning

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:31.000
I want to help you become successful

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:33.020
in the first years of your career.

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:35.400
This video is all about consulting.

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:38.540
It covers what I believe
it is extremely valuable

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:41.340
and helpful to start
off your business career

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:43.220
as a consultant even though

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:45.700
if you actually wanna do
something else in the long-term

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:47.810
and becoming a consultant is not something

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:49.250
that you plan to do forever.

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:51.880
So if you take any value
out of this video at all,

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:54.650
please press the like button
for the YouTube algorithm

00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:57.240
and also subscribe and
hit the notification bell

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:00.640
to stay up-to-date and receive
all the regular content

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:02.400
that I'm putting out there for you.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:03.233
At the moment,

00:02:03.233 --> 00:02:06.830
I'm releasing at least one
video every single Saturday.

00:02:06.830 --> 00:02:07.740
And in many weeks,

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:10.390
there's going even to be a
second video for you guys.

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:13.210
So if you are graduating
from university soon,

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:15.580
you will likely ask yourself the question,

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:17.440
what should be the first job?

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:20.210
What should be the first
role that I should take

00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:21.950
when I now start my career?

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:23.770
What is the wise career move,

00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:25.550
the first thing that I should start,

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:27.320
the first job that I should take?

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:29.650
And when I graduated
from my master program

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:31.160
at the London School of Economics,

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:33.730
I asked myself the same question.

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:36.180
And in my mind I bid in a stylized way,

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:39.560
I saw four options that you can
take as a business graduate.

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:43.560
You can either go into consulting,
you can go into banking,

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:46.960
you can work in industry or
you can start a start-up.

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:49.270
Of course, this is grossly simplified,

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:50.690
but if you break it down,

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:52.420
this is pretty much what you can do.

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:53.760
These are your options.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:57.230
So let's briefly go over the
startup and the banking choice.

00:02:57.230 --> 00:03:01.220
I believe that these two choices
are really specific choices

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:04.740
to people who's passion it is
to do exactly these things.

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:06.280
So if you want to do a start up,

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:08.280
if you want to become an entrepreneur,

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:09.330
you're probably not thinking

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:11.700
about whether you should
take on an industry job.

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:15.020
Most entrepreneurs I know they
just have it in your blood.

00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:16.410
If you wanna start a business,

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:19.130
if you wanna become an
entrepreneur, do a start up,

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:20.410
there's no other options for you.

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:22.890
And in this video, I'm not going in to try

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:24.760
to convince you to do something else.

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:26.930
I believe doing a startup is amazing.

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:28.190
If this is how you're taking,

00:03:28.190 --> 00:03:30.840
if this is what your
passion is, then go for it.

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:33.770
I fully have your back
go all in, this is great.

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:36.510
And even though on the one
side it's completely different,

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:39.330
on the other side, kind of
similar to that is banking.

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:40.270
From my experience,

00:03:40.270 --> 00:03:42.400
there's a special type
of business students,

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:44.730
a special type of people and personalities

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:46.730
who wanna go down the banking path

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:50.200
and even though banking now is
probably a bit less relevant

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:52.690
to many people than it
was roughly 10 years ago

00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:54.840
when I graduated from my master program,

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:57.440
banking still can be a
great career option for you.

00:03:57.440 --> 00:03:59.510
I have many friends who
work in investment banks,

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:01.370
or private equity, or similar role

00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:02.930
and they very much enjoy it.

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:05.240
And of course, it can be highly attractive

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:06.770
from a financial side as well.

00:04:06.770 --> 00:04:08.780
So startup and banking for this video,

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:10.290
I wanna a bit put aside,

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:13.180
because I believe while these
are very viable options,

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:14.810
either you wanna do it or you don't.

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:16.610
So the more interesting question

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:18.790
where I see people struggle with,

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:20.480
is for the other two sectors,

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:22.980
it's for consulting or for an industry.

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:24.490
So if you are a young graduate,

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:27.000
usually should you rather
pick the consulting

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:28.110
or the industry path?

00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:30.910
And just to be clear here on
terminology with industry,

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:34.280
I mean the more regular
standard business companies

00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:35.760
across all industries.

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:38.660
So let it be automotive, let
it be advanced industries,

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:42.710
let it be retail, pharma, oil
and gas, telecommunication.

00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:45.750
All of this is what I summarized
under the industry label.

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:48.940
So how does a typical industry starter job

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:51.890
compare to a typical
consulting starter job,

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:53.630
and I know now that in the comments

00:04:53.630 --> 00:04:55.100
people will write that of course

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:57.840
there's a huge diversity of jobs,

00:04:57.840 --> 00:04:59.500
both in industry and consulting,

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:01.420
and yes, you're completely right.

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:03.320
But I just try to generalize here a bit

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:06.410
because I do believe that many
of the roles within industry

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:07.787
and that within the consulting

00:05:07.787 --> 00:05:09.530
are pretty similar and comparable.

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:12.760
So in a typical industry role,
you start in one department.

00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:15.130
So you will either base
the business development,

00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:19.090
or maybe managerial accounting,
or production, or sales,

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:21.620
and then you work in
that team for a time span

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:22.930
of several years.

00:05:22.930 --> 00:05:25.360
You will be dedicated to fixed team,

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:27.430
you will have your one supervisor,

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:29.560
and then the game for you is pretty much

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:33.190
growing into this role really
becoming a part of the team,

00:05:33.190 --> 00:05:36.420
and then becoming a part of
the day-to-day operations

00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:37.300
of the business

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:39.970
and trying to really move
the business forward,

00:05:39.970 --> 00:05:42.230
making an impact in the business

00:05:42.230 --> 00:05:43.830
and every day that you worked out.

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:46.350
So how does this compare to consulting?

00:05:46.350 --> 00:05:48.140
Well, and if I talk about consulting

00:05:48.140 --> 00:05:49.940
I of course, especially mean

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:52.010
the large strategy consulting firms

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:54.230
like BCG, Bain or McKinsey,

00:05:54.230 --> 00:05:55.740
where you are usually in a setting

00:05:55.740 --> 00:05:57.370
where you work in a very small team

00:05:57.370 --> 00:06:00.650
of two, three or four people
on the ground for one client.

00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:02.790
A typical project will
go on for a duration

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:04.370
of two to five months,

00:06:04.370 --> 00:06:06.340
and then project for
project you will usually

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:09.300
change functions, change
industries, change clients

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:11.120
and then over the course of several years

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:13.630
get exposure to many of
these different situations.

00:06:13.630 --> 00:06:16.650
By then over time after your
two, three, four years down

00:06:16.650 --> 00:06:17.640
into your consulting role,

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:19.780
if you will specialize
more and more generally

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:22.180
on one industry to then
really become an expert

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:23.250
in one of these fields.

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:26.460
So while no doubt there
are disadvantages as well

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:27.920
when working in consulting.

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:29.610
In this video, I will argue

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:32.700
that I believe for most people out there,

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:34.620
who are a young business graduate

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:36.160
and are looking to make a mark

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:37.860
in the business world in the long-term.

00:06:37.860 --> 00:06:39.580
For most of these people,

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:43.900
it is the best choice to start
in a strategy consulting firm

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:46.270
such as McKinsey, Bain or BCG,

00:06:46.270 --> 00:06:48.270
if you're looking for the first job

00:06:48.270 --> 00:06:49.690
that you can take in your career.

00:06:49.690 --> 00:06:52.330
So let me tell you five strong reasons

00:06:52.330 --> 00:06:54.320
why I believe that this is the case.

00:06:54.320 --> 00:06:57.610
So the first reason that I
see is the size of a team.

00:06:57.610 --> 00:07:01.340
If you work at McKinsey,
or BCG, typical team size

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:03.140
is two to four people.

00:07:03.140 --> 00:07:05.950
On a typical project there
will be one project lead

00:07:05.950 --> 00:07:06.840
on the ground,

00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:10.200
and then to associate
supporting him at the client.

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:11.320
If you start as a consultant,

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:13.560
you will from the first week on

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:15.460
be staffed on a client project

00:07:15.460 --> 00:07:18.510
and will become one of these three members

00:07:18.510 --> 00:07:19.530
of your project team.

00:07:19.530 --> 00:07:22.080
Then usually what happens
is that the project lead

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:25.470
will divide the project
into different work streams.

00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:28.310
So pretty much packages of
work that need to be done

00:07:28.310 --> 00:07:30.680
and then distribute them
to all the team members,

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:33.160
so each of the associates and
the project leader himself

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:37.080
will have a certain set of tasks
that he is responsible for.

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:39.640
So imagine there's a company
with two business units

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:42.630
and as a BCG consultant,
now you are being asked

00:07:42.630 --> 00:07:45.640
to identify cost improvement potentials

00:07:45.640 --> 00:07:47.460
for these two business units.

00:07:47.460 --> 00:07:48.293
So in such a project,

00:07:48.293 --> 00:07:51.470
what will typically happen is
that there are two associates,

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:54.880
each associate is responsible
for one of the business units

00:07:54.880 --> 00:07:55.957
and then there's the project lead

00:07:55.957 --> 00:07:59.220
who will take care of some
maybe minor tasks left and right

00:07:59.220 --> 00:08:01.950
and of course, is responsible
for the overall quality

00:08:01.950 --> 00:08:03.401
of the output of the team.

00:08:03.401 --> 00:08:06.200
And what you will quickly realize
as such a young consultant

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:09.210
is that from early on, you will be alone,

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:11.950
sitting in meetings with senior clients

00:08:11.950 --> 00:08:15.480
of this business units with
pretty much work on yourself,

00:08:15.480 --> 00:08:18.150
pushing forward the topics
that you need to do.

00:08:18.150 --> 00:08:20.990
And if you for whatever
reason failed to do that,

00:08:20.990 --> 00:08:22.750
if you're not able to do that,

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:25.030
the whole team will struggle a lot,

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:27.480
because obviously the other associate

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:30.350
cannot also take care of
your whole business unit,

00:08:30.350 --> 00:08:32.450
because he is already highly utilized

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:33.700
with the work that he is doing.

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:36.240
And the project lead of
course, has many things to do,

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:39.200
and yes, for sure he will
help you and cover you

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:42.040
but he cannot pick up all
the slack of your work,

00:08:42.040 --> 00:08:43.010
if you're not doing it.

00:08:43.010 --> 00:08:45.050
So what this means is that from early on,

00:08:45.050 --> 00:08:48.360
you would be a critical
fundamental part of the team

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:51.950
and the whole team will
automatically rely on you

00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:54.180
getting the job done and doing good work.

00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:56.580
And trust me that this is vastly different

00:08:56.580 --> 00:08:57.630
from working in an industry,

00:08:57.630 --> 00:09:00.310
where usually you are part of a big team,

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:03.560
you have 10, 20, 30, 40 other people

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:04.890
working in your department.

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:06.110
And then as a new joiner

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:09.030
maybe they transfer a
few minor tasks to you

00:09:09.030 --> 00:09:09.977
that you then can work on.

00:09:09.977 --> 00:09:14.090
But in most of these roles
it's not a real serious problem

00:09:14.090 --> 00:09:16.390
if you for whatever reasons struggle

00:09:16.390 --> 00:09:18.830
because there will be other
people who can help you out.

00:09:18.830 --> 00:09:20.400
If it's really not working out,

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:23.340
they can likely also completely
cover all your tasks,

00:09:23.340 --> 00:09:24.710
especially in the beginning,

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:27.150
to give you some time to
really grow into your role

00:09:27.150 --> 00:09:28.520
in the first year or so.

00:09:28.520 --> 00:09:29.870
In consulting it's different.

00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:33.450
You will be expected to grow
into your role within weeks.

00:09:33.450 --> 00:09:34.540
And this very much feels

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:36.780
like being thrown into the cold water

00:09:36.780 --> 00:09:40.020
and it can sometimes be quite
a frightening experience

00:09:40.020 --> 00:09:41.580
for a new business joiner,

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:44.460
but this is exactly why the learning curve

00:09:44.460 --> 00:09:46.140
in consulting is so high,

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:49.340
and why you will learn such
a tremendous amount of things

00:09:49.340 --> 00:09:52.560
after working for consulting
within only one or two years.

00:09:52.560 --> 00:09:55.640
It is a learning experience
that is pretty much unparalleled

00:09:55.640 --> 00:09:57.860
in almost all interesting jobs out there.

00:09:57.860 --> 00:10:00.470
Reason number two is the
exposure that you get

00:10:00.470 --> 00:10:02.327
to many different leadership styles.

00:10:02.327 --> 00:10:03.890
And this is something that I believe

00:10:03.890 --> 00:10:06.320
many people significantly undervalue

00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:08.710
when they are thinking about
joining a job in an industry.

00:10:08.710 --> 00:10:11.780
'Cause in industry you're
part of a fixed team.

00:10:11.780 --> 00:10:14.380
And this means that your
supervisor or your team lead

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:15.910
will usually be constant,

00:10:15.910 --> 00:10:18.420
maybe fixed for a long period of time.

00:10:18.420 --> 00:10:21.210
So if you're there for three
years, four years, five years,

00:10:21.210 --> 00:10:22.230
maybe even longer,

00:10:22.230 --> 00:10:24.320
it could be the case that all the time

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:27.260
you work with and for
the very same team lead

00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:29.170
or team manager the whole time,

00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:31.180
and why this of course has some advantages

00:10:31.180 --> 00:10:33.420
and there can be a deep
mentoring relationship

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:34.330
coming out of that,

00:10:34.330 --> 00:10:36.360
the big downside is that you get exposure

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:38.770
to only this one leadership style.

00:10:38.770 --> 00:10:40.290
And this could not be more different

00:10:40.290 --> 00:10:42.570
than what you will experience
when you work in consulting.

00:10:42.570 --> 00:10:45.250
In consulting every two to five months

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:46.727
you will work on a new project

00:10:46.727 --> 00:10:47.763
and this usually involves

00:10:47.763 --> 00:10:50.620
that you will work with
a new project lead.

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:51.810
And but of course, it is true

00:10:51.810 --> 00:10:54.460
that there is a certain
homogeneous culture

00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:57.220
in a consulting firm like BCG or McKinsey,

00:10:57.220 --> 00:10:59.120
the truth is also that still

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:01.050
the leadership styles of the people

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:02.497
are sometimes vastly different.

00:11:02.497 --> 00:11:04.080
The way your project lead

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:06.320
will handle difficult client meetings,

00:11:06.320 --> 00:11:08.150
the way your project lead will react

00:11:08.150 --> 00:11:11.050
when the more senior partner
of the consulting firm

00:11:11.050 --> 00:11:13.420
pushes the project team
in a certain direction.

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:15.520
But if he believes that this
is not the right direction,

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:17.860
how he will push back
to the senior leadership

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:20.220
will be vastly different
among the different people.

00:11:20.220 --> 00:11:21.530
How we handles the team.

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:22.820
How he motivates you.

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:24.370
How he interacts with you.

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:27.370
All of this will be vastly
different from person to person.

00:11:27.370 --> 00:11:29.900
And as a consultant sitting
on the receiving end

00:11:29.900 --> 00:11:31.960
of this internal leadership that you get,

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:35.630
this gives you the opportunity
to self reflect a lot.

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:38.490
Because this is as if there
would be lots of experiments

00:11:38.490 --> 00:11:40.120
happening just in front of you.

00:11:40.120 --> 00:11:42.480
You can watch all these
project leads of you

00:11:42.480 --> 00:11:44.150
trying out different things,

00:11:44.150 --> 00:11:46.620
different styles and
seeing what is working,

00:11:46.620 --> 00:11:47.477
what is not working.

00:11:47.477 --> 00:11:49.900
And of course, you will
frequently see these people

00:11:49.900 --> 00:11:52.280
do certain things, and the
end you will tell yourself,

00:11:52.280 --> 00:11:54.590
well, probably I would
have handled this situation

00:11:54.590 --> 00:11:55.550
a different way.

00:11:55.550 --> 00:11:57.920
Probably the way that he handled this

00:11:57.920 --> 00:11:59.370
didn't really work out that well,

00:11:59.370 --> 00:12:01.150
he should probably have
done something else.

00:12:01.150 --> 00:12:03.250
And the fact that you see
all these different styles

00:12:03.250 --> 00:12:05.380
in the short amount of time

00:12:05.380 --> 00:12:07.700
really enables you to ask yourself,

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:10.900
what is the type of leader
that you want to become?

00:12:10.900 --> 00:12:13.430
What is the leadership style
that you want to adopt?

00:12:13.430 --> 00:12:15.730
And the exposure to all
these different styles

00:12:15.730 --> 00:12:18.650
from my experience is extremely valuable.

00:12:18.650 --> 00:12:21.940
And this is something that
you would just not get at all

00:12:21.940 --> 00:12:24.530
if you work in an industry
or in another position,

00:12:24.530 --> 00:12:26.070
where your boss, your supervisor

00:12:26.070 --> 00:12:29.030
will be the very same person
for a long amount of time.

00:12:29.030 --> 00:12:31.087
And this now leads me
to reason number three,

00:12:31.087 --> 00:12:33.900
and this is that an industry
often highly dependent

00:12:33.900 --> 00:12:35.500
on a small amount of people,

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:37.860
and especially your direct supervisor.

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:39.560
How your work is evaluated?

00:12:39.560 --> 00:12:42.690
Whether you're considered as
a strong performer or not?

00:12:42.690 --> 00:12:45.240
What your internal
performance rating would be?

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:49.650
An industry will very much
depend on your direct supervisor.

00:12:49.650 --> 00:12:51.320
And of course, this can be a big plus

00:12:51.320 --> 00:12:53.800
if you happen to get along
really well with a person

00:12:53.800 --> 00:12:54.970
but on the other hand side,

00:12:54.970 --> 00:12:57.530
if you do not get along
with a person really well

00:12:57.530 --> 00:12:59.940
this can become a huge problem for you.

00:12:59.940 --> 00:13:02.360
Because pretty much the
only choice that you have

00:13:02.360 --> 00:13:05.480
is either transitional
roles within the company,

00:13:05.480 --> 00:13:07.700
which is often easier said than done,

00:13:07.700 --> 00:13:10.050
or change your job to a
completely new employer,

00:13:10.050 --> 00:13:12.470
which of course, is not
something that you often wanna do

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:14.900
if you're just within the first
year or so of your career.

00:13:14.900 --> 00:13:16.950
So if you compare that now to consulting,

00:13:16.950 --> 00:13:19.340
in consulting you usually change the teams

00:13:19.340 --> 00:13:20.720
every couple of months.

00:13:20.720 --> 00:13:22.530
And this means that if you happen to work

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:24.060
with a project lead for whom you

00:13:24.060 --> 00:13:26.190
and probably then also
the project lead realizes

00:13:26.190 --> 00:13:27.780
that this isn't really a good fit.

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:30.410
In a few months, he would change
the team, it's a new game.

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:32.200
There will be a new
person who can work with

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:34.760
then over time, you
will have a good network

00:13:34.760 --> 00:13:38.070
of project leads, of partners
with whom you enjoy working,

00:13:38.070 --> 00:13:39.960
and then hopefully also on the other side,

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:41.690
they will enjoy working with you.

00:13:41.690 --> 00:13:45.750
And then you can actively try
to seek out working together

00:13:45.750 --> 00:13:47.850
with these people more and more.

00:13:47.850 --> 00:13:49.650
They then appreciate you as well,

00:13:49.650 --> 00:13:51.780
they of course will be more
than happy to work with you

00:13:51.780 --> 00:13:52.860
again and again.

00:13:52.860 --> 00:13:56.150
And by this you can really
build your own community.

00:13:56.150 --> 00:13:59.530
You can build your own firm
within the consulting firm.

00:13:59.530 --> 00:14:00.900
And in consulting this is then

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:04.300
how mutually beneficial
mentorship relationships

00:14:04.300 --> 00:14:05.350
can be built.

00:14:05.350 --> 00:14:08.590
Because you want to work again
with these project leads,

00:14:08.590 --> 00:14:10.320
the partners want to work again with you

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:12.950
because they know that you
are a rockstar, you are loyal,

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:15.170
you will do great work for
them on their projects.

00:14:15.170 --> 00:14:16.560
This is really completely different

00:14:16.560 --> 00:14:17.860
to how it works in industry.

00:14:17.860 --> 00:14:20.970
Reason number four is the
sheer amount of experiences

00:14:20.970 --> 00:14:22.080
that you get from working

00:14:22.080 --> 00:14:25.800
for a large strategy consulting
firm, like McKinsey or BCG

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:27.230
when you start out with your career.

00:14:27.230 --> 00:14:29.170
During my six years at McKinsey,

00:14:29.170 --> 00:14:31.180
I've been involved in lots of projects

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:33.920
covering all types of
industries and functions.

00:14:33.920 --> 00:14:35.950
I have been involved in large M&amp;As

00:14:35.950 --> 00:14:37.803
so mergers and acquisitions transactions.

00:14:37.803 --> 00:14:41.160
I've been working on major cost
and revenue transformations

00:14:41.160 --> 00:14:42.850
of large blue chip companies.

00:14:42.850 --> 00:14:44.650
I've worked on all kinds of countries

00:14:44.650 --> 00:14:46.330
within and outside of Europe.

00:14:46.330 --> 00:14:48.180
I work together with buying departments

00:14:48.180 --> 00:14:50.750
helping them improve their
direct and indirect spend.

00:14:50.750 --> 00:14:52.390
I developed new sales strategies

00:14:52.390 --> 00:14:54.110
for large chemicals companies.

00:14:54.110 --> 00:14:57.000
You're pricing structures
for retail companies.

00:14:57.000 --> 00:15:00.130
I evaluated the CAPEX pipeline
for automotive suppliers.

00:15:00.130 --> 00:15:02.210
And many, many, many more things.

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:04.310
I would argue that it's just impossible

00:15:04.310 --> 00:15:07.270
to get that amount of
experience in that little time

00:15:07.270 --> 00:15:10.200
if you work in pretty much
any regular industry role.

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:11.970
And last but not least is the exposure

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:15.050
to C-level management of
large blue chip companies

00:15:15.050 --> 00:15:16.200
that you get early on.

00:15:16.200 --> 00:15:19.030
On many projects you will work
closely together with CEOs,

00:15:19.030 --> 00:15:21.307
CFOs of large companies.

00:15:21.307 --> 00:15:23.690
You would work together
with business unit heads

00:15:23.690 --> 00:15:26.540
with really senior level
management of the companies.

00:15:26.540 --> 00:15:29.360
These are people that if you
work in a normal department,

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:31.060
in a normal industry role

00:15:31.060 --> 00:15:34.240
you might never even speak to face-to-face

00:15:34.240 --> 00:15:36.220
in the first years of your career.

00:15:36.220 --> 00:15:39.180
And to the contrary, as a
McKinsey or BCG consultant,

00:15:39.180 --> 00:15:41.080
you sit together in a room with them

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:43.810
and work together with
them on the most pressing

00:15:43.810 --> 00:15:47.260
top of mind issues that
these C-level executives

00:15:47.260 --> 00:15:48.380
have in their head.

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:50.890
And they seek your
expertise, they respect you

00:15:50.890 --> 00:15:52.880
and they closely work together with you

00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:56.690
to solve these high priority
issues of their companies.

00:15:56.690 --> 00:15:59.080
This is just unparalleled,
this will not be possible

00:15:59.080 --> 00:16:00.870
in most industry roles.

00:16:00.870 --> 00:16:02.710
So looking at these five reasons,

00:16:02.710 --> 00:16:06.330
I honestly believe that
pretty much independent

00:16:06.330 --> 00:16:08.530
of what you wanna do in the long-term,

00:16:08.530 --> 00:16:11.550
you will benefit from having
worked a couple of years

00:16:11.550 --> 00:16:14.150
in a large strategy consulting firm,

00:16:14.150 --> 00:16:16.000
such as McKinsey or BCG.

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:19.600
But also do not get me wrong,
consulting is not perfect.

00:16:19.600 --> 00:16:21.040
It's not a fairy tale.

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:23.070
It's no lala land that you work in

00:16:23.070 --> 00:16:25.330
and everything is just great and amazing.

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:27.480
There are some significant downsides

00:16:27.480 --> 00:16:29.117
of working in consulting as well.

00:16:29.117 --> 00:16:31.650
And here I'm not even talking
about work life balance,

00:16:31.650 --> 00:16:33.250
but rather specific learnings

00:16:33.250 --> 00:16:36.110
that I believe are crucial
and absolutely needed

00:16:36.110 --> 00:16:38.160
for you to be successful in the long-term,

00:16:38.160 --> 00:16:40.680
but which you will not
develop at all in consulting.

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:42.420
So this could actually be another video

00:16:42.420 --> 00:16:44.070
me talking about what the things are

00:16:44.070 --> 00:16:46.490
that you will for sure
not learn in consulting.

00:16:46.490 --> 00:16:48.420
So if this is something
that would interest you,

00:16:48.420 --> 00:16:50.280
please let me know below in the comments.

00:16:50.280 --> 00:16:52.240
And I'll likely make another video on that

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:53.310
in the couple of weeks.

00:16:53.310 --> 00:16:55.420
But just because there are some things

00:16:55.420 --> 00:16:57.450
which you will not learn in consulting,

00:16:57.450 --> 00:16:59.390
I also believe that it is important

00:16:59.390 --> 00:17:00.927
that after a couple of years,

00:17:00.927 --> 00:17:03.320
you're thinking about making a transition

00:17:03.320 --> 00:17:07.060
and going into more
operational, more hands on role,

00:17:07.060 --> 00:17:09.890
your development path of
becoming a go to waivers

00:17:09.890 --> 00:17:13.010
business professional of
becoming a good general manager

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:14.410
would just not be completed.

00:17:14.410 --> 00:17:16.470
If you're just working
in consulting you need

00:17:16.470 --> 00:17:19.900
the small operational line
management experience this way.

00:17:19.900 --> 00:17:22.000
So what is your thinking on all of this?

00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:24.280
Let me know your opinion
below in the comments.

00:17:24.280 --> 00:17:26.130
Probably some of you
thinking that I'm wrong

00:17:26.130 --> 00:17:28.143
and consulting is not
the best role to start

00:17:28.143 --> 00:17:30.250
as a young business professionals.

00:17:30.250 --> 00:17:32.560
So very happy to have an
open conversation here.

00:17:32.560 --> 00:17:34.340
Let me know what your thoughts are,

00:17:34.340 --> 00:17:36.660
and I will give you an
answer below in the comments.

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:39.680
And again, if you took any
value out of this video at all,

00:17:39.680 --> 00:17:42.090
please hit the like button
for the YouTube algorithm

00:17:42.090 --> 00:17:44.190
and also hit the subscribe button,

00:17:44.190 --> 00:17:46.440
as well as activate the notification bell

00:17:46.440 --> 00:17:47.920
to stay informed and up-to-date

00:17:47.920 --> 00:17:49.930
on all the future content
I've planned for you.

